cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the benchmark it produces, please cite the paper
  below rather than the repository alone. The repository is the artefact; the
  paper is where the method and the measurements are described.
title: >-
  Kayenta AI Canary Judge: a model-agnostic remote judge and benchmark for
  automated canary analysis
abstract: >-
  A configurable remote judge for Kayenta that produces a canary verdict from a
  large language model or a vision-language model, three explicit hybrid policies
  that combine it with the genuine NetflixACAJudge verdict, a tuned statistical
  ensemble baseline, and a seeded nine-family fault-injection benchmark of 180
  labelled scenarios with the harness that scores every judge over it.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/VladStefanDieaconu/kayenta-ai-canary-judge"
keywords:
  - automated canary analysis
  - continuous delivery
  - progressive delivery
  - Mann-Whitney U test
  - large language models
  - vision-language models
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - anomaly detection
  - site reliability engineering
